{"aliases":[],"authors":[],"details":{"availability":"Ungated Hub dataset with JSONL trajectories and archived screenshots","dataset_profile":{"counts":[{"basis":"reported","evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md","population":"Capability set","qualifier":"exact","unit":"trajectories","value":4344},{"basis":"reported","evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md","population":"Capability set","qualifier":"exact","unit":"interaction steps","value":68140},{"basis":"reported","evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md","population":"Safety-v2 set","qualifier":"exact","unit":"trajectories","value":541},{"basis":"reported","evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md","population":"Safety-v2 set","qualifier":"exact","unit":"interaction steps","value":3486},{"basis":"reported","evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md","population":"legacy Safety archive","qualifier":"exact","unit":"trajectories","value":6152},{"basis":"reported","evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md","population":"legacy Safety archive","qualifier":"exact","unit":"interaction steps","value":88496}],"evidence_urls":["https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md","https://arxiv.org/html/2605.06230v2"],"formats":["JSONL","ZIP image archives","tar.gz image archives"],"modalities":["screenshots","instructions","actions","action descriptions"],"notes":"Counts are publisher-reported on the card. The card's headline 4,885 trajectories and 71,626 steps cover Capability plus Safety-v2 only. The Safactory report's 10,496 trajectories match Capability plus the legacy Safety archive, but its 158,196 steps do not equal the card's step totals for those sets. A trajectory is a multi-step episode; screenshot counts use a different unit.","splits":["capability/train","safety/train","safety_v2/train"],"supervision":["computer-use trajectories","task-success labels","safety-outcome labels","safe-refusal examples"]},"disabled":false,"download_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/tree/74deb768ee16733b952b789e91b69e7450df5dea","gated":false,"hub_id":"AI45Research/SATraj-OS","release_revision":"74deb768ee16733b952b789e91b69e7450df5dea"},"environments":["desktop"],"evidence":[{"method":"editorial_primary_review","retrieved_at":"2026-10-18T11:15:59Z","role":"primary","sha256":"2e23775770af343f07319036f671ad5561ec387fcbcc2f7ea9199bf90494d977","supports":["name","kind","summary","environments","topics","scope","notes","relations","details.dataset_profile","licenses.data"],"url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md"},{"method":"editorial_primary_review","retrieved_at":"2026-10-18T11:16:00Z","role":"primary","sha256":"9afd95cd02de90cb4fab79a80810f5858409128e23a19b6913b79571ea5766f5","supports":["identity","release_status","details.release_revision","details.hub_id","details.gated","details.disabled","details.download_url"],"url":"https://huggingface.co/api/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS"},{"method":"editorial_primary_review","retrieved_at":"2026-10-18T11:16:01Z","role":"primary","sha256":"f2b9696b13f7052a31f460675dd19e406485816dd284892378c2e281ec3d3d16","supports":["notes","details.dataset_profile"],"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2605.06230v2"},{"method":"huggingface_card","retrieved_at":"2026-10-18T11:15:59Z","role":"primary","sha256":"2e23775770af343f07319036f671ad5561ec387fcbcc2f7ea9199bf90494d977","supports":["licenses.data"],"url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md"}],"id":"url:73b9b17648ea7af7aa8f","identifiers":{},"kind":"dataset","last_verified_at":"2026-10-18T11:15:59Z","licenses":{"code":null,"data":{"basis":"publisher model/dataset card metadata","declared":"apache-2.0","retrieved_at":"2026-10-18T11:15:59Z","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS/raw/main/README.md"},"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS"}],"name":"SATraj-OS","notes":"The ungated Hub repository (revision 74deb768) publishes trajectories.jsonl files with zipped or tarred step screenshots in three configs: Capability (tasks from SCOPE-Gen), Safety-v2 (safe completions and refusals on attack-injected Capability tasks) and a legacy Safety archive generated through RiOSWorld rollouts that keeps risky outcomes. Each record has chat-format messages whose assistant turns hold an action description and a coordinate action, plus success, safety, reward and attack fields. The card declares Apache-2.0 for the data; screenshots show third-party desktop applications whose own terms are not addressed. Thunderbird and VLC capability files are present outside the capability config. The Safactory report (arXiv 2605.06230, v2) describes SATraj-OS as produced with its OSGym environment and reports 10,496 trajectories and 158,196 steps. That paper is not yet in the retained archive, so no paper relation is recorded.","published_at":null,"relations":[],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Desktop computer-use trajectories with per-step screenshots and success, safety and attack labels, split into capability runs, safe-completion and refusal runs, and a legacy RiOSWorld-derived safety archive.","task_classes":["R01.05.02.01"],"topics":["data-generation","safety-security","imitation-learning"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI45Research/SATraj-OS"}
